emy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{-\\pi /4})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/state.json" "file_sha256" "f26009d6e94d07cbf154d89130c1d7d423b01243d5d77ac4c27f2b79e765a456" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{e}^{\\pi /4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/state.json" "file_sha256" "f26009d6e94d07cbf154d89130c1d7d423b01243d5d77ac4c27f2b79e765a456" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /4}-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/state.json" "file_sha256" "f26009d6e94d07cbf154d89130c1d7d423b01243d5d77ac4c27f2b79e765a456" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/state.json" "file_sha256" "f26009d6e94d07cbf154d89130c1d7d423b01243d5d77ac4c27f2b79e765a456" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/085be1e624ae99afee256d2a9591f17d2f33f688364b6e59fdcd7c415206bda7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/state.json" "file_sha256" "f26009d6e94d07cbf154d89130c1d7d423b01243d5d77ac4c27f2b79e765a456" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta {|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/state.json" "file_sha256" "f26009d6e94d07cbf154d89130c1d7d423b01243d5d77ac4c27f2b79e765a456" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "126a5613e9d54d7b3f561384301afea7c550865541449bfed6cdb2fdc8291a97" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/state.json" "file_sha256" "f26009d6e94d07cbf154d89130c1d7d423b01243d5d77ac4c27f2b79e765a456" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/e5647c0f19727d1e626e637464cc57444e0bc0f2f8e99a4afd15d3c3631dc3f0.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the arc length of the polar curve $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi,$ shown in blue in the diagram above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/example-7400.json" "file_sha256" "28619c4d4743f4c652ae2549f40de343a6bc6f724b13059b8072ffa6dbc2bf98" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} =-7\\cos(7\\theta)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}+(-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+49{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+1+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/example-7400.json" "file_sha256" "28619c4d4743f4c652ae2549f40de343a6bc6f724b13059b8072ffa6dbc2bf98" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/0bb9e5e7315d4bcd5fc21700fdd2597f6d9b585a109145de53c6f94e9530eabf.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi$ (shown in blue in the picture above)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/example-641.json" "file_sha256" "d0167d64c4c6e7ff59561f7df2ef5270c1a704998c8d2f2f9140715d7d16fdff" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now use the half-angle formula $1-\\cos\\theta =2\\sin^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$ to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={-4\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/example-641.json" "file_sha256" "d0167d64c4c6e7ff59561f7df2ef5270c1a704998c8d2f2f9140715d7d16fdff" "basis" 2233 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-103832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b1ed19fd4a8c9d1e603759e8dfd614a9b19cf8538c17e1fc27da327e60f3985"} {"question" "q-103832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))^{2}+(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b1ed19fd4a8c9d1e603759e8dfd614a9b19cf8538c17e1fc27da327e60f3985"} {"question" "q-103832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refe